window.docContents[173].resolve({"/Types-and-expressions/Variable/#Core-C______--Types-and-expressions--Variable":{"contents":"The variable denotes the location the environment assigns to it, and the store does not change. A variable that a lambda captures by copy is read only in , so it denotes no location for the type checker, and no assignment reaches it. Inside a member body an unqualified field of this also denotes a location, rule LocVarField of , with the typing rule T-LocVarField. The other expressions that denote a location, *e, e.f and e->f, are the nodes of the last section. An element v[i] of a vector is a use of the library, .The set  holds the variables of  captured by copy inside a lambda, TEnv.isConst.\n\nReading  is reading . The premise  fails for a location that left the store, so that read has no derivation and the evaluator gives error. Inside a member body  may be a field of this, rule T-VarField of , and the first premise of Var then holds by LocVarField.\n\n","context":"Core C++\u0009Types and expressions","header":"3.2. Variable","id":"/Types-and-expressions/Variable/#Core-C______--Types-and-expressions--Variable"}});